cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Semantic Afterlife: Long-Run Dynamics of Large Language Models Beyond the
  Context Horizon
message: >-
  If you use this software or its artifacts, please cite it. Once the manuscript
  is released, cite the paper instead and this repository as the software.
type: software
authors:
  - name: llm-semantic-afterlife contributors
repository-code: https://github.com/AdamCage/llm-semantic-afterlife
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-30"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - dynamical systems
  - Markov state models
  - semantic drift
  - context window
  - metastability
  - non-equilibrium dynamics
abstract: >-
  A reproducible experimental framework for studying the long-run semantic
  dynamics of large language models generating freely under an imposed finite
  sliding context window. Once the initial prompt has been evicted from the
  window, the trajectory is characterised as a stochastic dynamical system:
  semantic memory decay (semantic half-life), mean squared displacement scaling,
  metastable macrostates from non-reversible Markov state models, probability
  currents, and the dependence of all of these on window size, temperature and
  model family.
